<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyrenaica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyrenaica is the eastern coastal region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, named after the ancient Greek city of Cyrene. It lay on the routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>. Under rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalawun">Qalawun</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> extended its control over Cyrenaica.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyrenaica.jpg" alt="Cyrenaica" width="316" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esemono; derivative work by Felitsata · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Cyrenaica_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
